    "Description": "The Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) is a protocol that allows individual devices on an IP network to get their own network configuration information, including an IP address, a subnet mask, and a broadcast address. The dhcp packages provide a relay agent and ISC DHCP service required to enable and administer DHCP on a network.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* dhcp-server: dhcp-server: Persistent denial of service due to buffer overflow via OMAPI (CVE-2026-18103)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* dhcpd dies constantly with \"Error allocating fallback interface: invalid argument\" (JIRA:RHEL-151420)\n\n* Attempt to free pointer that is inside a structure in get_hw_addr2 (JIRA:RHEL-235872)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 Release Notes linked from the References section.",
